  "$comment": "Farm & Charm's stove, a brick oven, turned as the block faces (front to the north). The station hides the block while it is used and shows it here as its burning block has it: the mouth in its front (x 3..13, y 8..12) over the grate, the firebox opening under it (x 6..11, y 1..5). The iron plate that shuts the mouth on the cold block is the door, hinged at its left edge; the stove bakes only with it shut. The grate slides out 7 px as the tray, with three places side by side in the middle of what is out (the stove's slots 1-3); the dish that is baked lies there too (slot 0); the fuel lies in the firebox, seen through its opening (slot 4): the firebox is an opening of its own under the door, where fuel is laid on and taken off at any time, as at every place, or let go over the tray. It is the stove in the world too, with nobody at it (the station hides the block wherever the scene is drawn): the stove looks the same with the station open or shut; further off the block and its own renderer are the stove. Blocks beside it stay in the picture (clear_view.blocks off), as at Hands-On Delight's oven.",
